      "writtenOn": "2021-08-12T02:23:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e initial value now set from TRNG\n\nwell, that\u0027s not enough. if an external user ever sees a direct value from fast_random, they can predict all following values. so, either (1) never use fast_randoms as-is w/o further one-way transformations or (2) mix them with TRNG-value that is never exposed (to illustrate the idea: imagine XORing all fast randoms with a value seeded from TRNG once).\n\nbut am I right that (1) never happens?",
      "parentUuid": "5fe65bf1_6c922092",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "cfb14a23f51d5fbdd336a61f90e889e220e93bea",
