      "writtenOn": "2021-08-12T04:15:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "next_fast_random is used for blinding/shredding stale data only. if DRBG fails, the caller will see this is the case ( and don\u0027t return successful return code for signing - https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/3087833/4/board/cr50/dcrypto/dcrypto_p256.c#840 - this is the only place where this function is currently used. I plan though to use it in FIPS-friendly U2F Generate/Sign since it\u0027s common code snippet.\nother use cases - replacement for memset(). It\u0027s just faster than rand() and allows code to run on host().",
